 "notes": "AC oscillation (time-dependent cosmic birefringence) search with SPT-3G 2019 data. Headline curve is the 'Smoothed SPT-3G 2019 limit' (dashed black line, Fig. 5), given analytically by Eq. (22): g_phi_gamma < 1.25e-12 GeV^-1 * (m_phi/1.0e-21 eV) * [sinc(m_phi/1.72e-19 eV)]^-1, with unnormalized sinc(x)=sin(x)/x. Points computed from Eq. (22) over the search band f=0.01-2.00 inverse-days (oscillation periods 100 days to 0.5 days), i.e. m_phi ~ 4.79e-22 to 9.57e-20 eV using m_phi = 2*pi*hbar/P. The near-flat-frequency approximation Eq. (23) gives g < 1.18e-12 GeV^-1*(m/1e-21 eV). Assumes axions are the full local DM at density 0.3 GeV/cm^3 (do not rescale). Paper's g_phi_gamma is taken as canonical g_agamma (F19 convention). Improves on BK22 by ~3.8x.",
